{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2246","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. lce4113 and Security Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Additionally, hacks are disabled for this problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are two hidden integers $$$b$$$ and $$$v$$$ such that $$$b \\in \\{0,1\\}$$$ and $$$0 \\le v \\lt 2^{30}.$$$ There is also a hidden operation $$$\\mathrm{ty},$$$ which is either $$$\\&$$$ or $$$|.$$$ Here, $$$\\&$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise AND operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". Additionally, $$$|$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your goal is to guess $$$b.$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The interaction proceeds as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" First, you send a value $$$x$$$ to the interactor, such that $$$0 \\le x \\lt 2^{30}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The interactor sends back $$$v\\,\\mathrm{ty}\\,x$$$. Formally, it will send back $$$o(v,x)$$$, where $$$$$$o(v,x) = \\begin{cases}v\\,\\&\\,x & \\mathrm{ty} = \\& \\\\ v\\,|\\,x & \\mathrm{ty} = |.\\end{cases}$$$$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" You then send two numbers $$$m_0$$$ and $$$m_1$$$, where $$$0 \\le m_0, m_1 \\lt 2^{30}.$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Finally, the interactor will send back $$$m_b \\oplus v,$$$ where $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the interaction, you have to output $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^5$$$). The description of the test cases follows. Note that this is the only initial input given."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, you need to output a single integer $$$x \\, (0 \\le x \\lt 2^{30})$$$ — the initial value to send to the interactor."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In response, you will receive a single integer $$$o\\,(0 \\le o \\lt 2^{30})$$$ — the result $$$o(v,x)$$$ of the operation $$$v\\,\\mathrm{ty}\\,x.$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next, you will send a single line containing two integers $$$m_0, m_1\\,(0 \\le m_0, m_1 \\lt 2^{30}).$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Finally, receive a single integer $$$r\\,(0 \\le r \\lt 2^{30})$$$ — the value of $$$m_b \\oplus v.$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the interactor is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"partially adaptive"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — in particular, the choice of $$$v$$$ may be determined by the initial input $$$x$$$, but "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all hidden values will be fixed after"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing each query do not forget to output the end of line and flush$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" verdict."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If, at any interaction step, you read $$$-1$$$ instead of valid data, your solution must exit immediately. This means that your solution will receive "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wrong answer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" because of an invalid query or any other mistake. Failing to exit can result in an arbitrary verdict because your solution will continue to read from a closed stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$To flush, use: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sys.stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see the documentation for other languages. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n\n0\n\n315\n\n3\n\n35\n\n5\n\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n\n314 159\n\n0\n\n3\n\n12 34\n\n1\n\n0\n\n0 0\n\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The example interaction proceeds as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interactor"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$3$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$3$$$ test cases."}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$2$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The solution chooses $$$x = 2$$$."}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"kind":"table